{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1506776-stat-blocks-in-city-books","id":1506776,"title":"Stat blocks in city books","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-03-28T12:18:22-07:00","id":1506776,"title":"Stat blocks in city books","content":"All of the city books I've seen have full stat blocks for npcs. Is this really the preference, or is it kind of a waste of space? Would abbreviated stat blocks with common dice pools be better for a city book, especially one with lots of npcs, or would you be disappointed if you got a book that only had abbreviated stats?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13542-shadowdragon","name":"Shadowdragon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-28T14:47:32-07:00","id":1506792,"title":"","content":"I don't think most readers would be disappointed. For instance, the dedicated citybook for Vampire the Requiem <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/2364/City-of-the-Damned-New-Orleans?affiliate_id=321987\" target=\"_blank\">City of the Damned: New Orleans</a> had the full stat blocks. My impression was that the game back then did have an eye on the expectations readers brought over from Vampire the Masquerade's &quot;by Night&quot; series. So probably, the stat block custom followed suit too.<br /> <br /> But it isn't necessarily a help for the storyteller. it might give too much information, and in some cases strange, incomplete or erronous stats might even give the storyteller some trouble.<br /> <br /> My impression is that Onyx Path has generally moved towards more descriptions, less stats, in their descriptions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27293,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27293-cabaal","user":"Cabaal","date":". 03-29-2023, 12:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27293-cabaal","name":"Cabaal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27293_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-28T17:25:43-07:00","id":1506807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cabaal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1506776-stat-blocks-in-city-books?p=1506792#post1506792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't most readers would be disappointed. For instance, the dedicated citybook for Vampire the Requiem <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/2364/City-of-the-Damned-New-Orleans?affiliate_id=321987\" target=\"_blank\">City of the Damned: New Orleans</a> had the full stat blocks. My impression was that the game back then did have an eye on the expectations readers brought over from Vampire the Masquerade's &quot;by Night&quot; series. So probably, the stat block custom followed suit too.<br /> <br /> But it isn't necessarily a help for the storyteller. it might give too much information, and in some cases strange, incomplete or erronous stats might even give the storyteller some trouble.<br /> <br /> My impression is that Onyx Path has generally moved towards more descriptions, less stats, in their descriptions.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess a matter of style preferences, or even simple habit, plays a hand at things too - in the covenantbooks themselves you'll find a mix of abbreviated stat blocks or fully stated ones in the NPCs, even though they are all supposed to be templates more than actual characters anyway. Both things are valid depending on the degree of detail one presents on a book NPC or its portrayal.<br /> <br /> And even a &quot;buggy&quot; portrayal of a character, whose stats make for an ill-fit with its background and the writing can be useful too, in that it makes the reader more attentive to consistency, detail and question what one is presented with or inspire different readings of a character by filling blanks between writing and stats among other things. I for one love tweaking and retooling book NPCs and add all kinds of new details and takes in the process.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-29T02:42:33-07:00","id":1506834,"title":"","content":"All the city books are first edition, with the reduced stat blocks from the CoD book I suspect new city books would use the new reduced stat blocks. That said it\u2019s not going to happen, second edition doesn\u2019t look likely to expand like first edition did.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-29T15:35:07-07:00","id":1506878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowdragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1506776-stat-blocks-in-city-books#post1506776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All of the city books I've seen have full stat blocks for npcs. Is this really the preference, or is it kind of a waste of space? Would abbreviated stat blocks with common dice pools be better for a city book, especially one with lots of npcs, or would you be disappointed if you got a book that only had abbreviated stats?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think I've ever seen an NPC with a reduced statblock in these books <i>ever</i>? And I would need an example of some otherwise case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-29T21:35:35-07:00","id":1506926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1506776-stat-blocks-in-city-books?p=1506878#post1506878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think I've ever seen an NPC with a reduced statblock in these books <i>ever</i>? And I would need an example of some otherwise case.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Now i'm in doubt personally - it has been years since i last checked either book, but would have to check New Orleans and Chicago on that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-31T00:04:37-07:00","id":1507025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1506776-stat-blocks-in-city-books?p=1506878#post1506878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think I've ever seen an NPC with a reduced statblock in these books <i>ever</i>? And I would need an example of some otherwise case.</div> </div> </div> </div>I haven't seen them in a city book (yet), but there are reduced stat blocks in the CoD core book for generic npcs. A couple days ago I decided to give the reduced stat block thing a try for the npcs in my chronicle and found that a lot of the time I was just giving skill scores anyway. The mafia hitman has a firearms dice pool of 10, which my mind immediately broke down into Dex 4, Firearms 5, rifle specialization. In the end I just decided to go with full size stat blocks, but only give what the character actually needs rather than fiddling with dozens of 1 and 2 dot stats. The hitman has firearms, stealth, a bit of brawl, and athletics, nothing else matters. It makes for very incomplete stat blocks, but npcs don't really need numbers assigned to everything. My biggest struggle right now is just figuring out what are good attribute totals for creatures of different power levels. What do attributes for a BP 8 vampire look like compared to a BP 2 vampire. Would there really be that much of a difference?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13542-shadowdragon","name":"Shadowdragon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-31T02:21:31-07:00","id":1507042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowdragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1506776-stat-blocks-in-city-books?p=1507025#post1507025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I haven't seen them in a city book (yet), but there are reduced stat blocks in the CoD core book for generic npcs. A couple days ago I decided to give the reduced stat block thing a try for the npcs in my chronicle and found that a lot of the time I was just giving skill scores anyway. The mafia hitman has a firearms dice pool of 10, which my mind immediately broke down into Dex 4, Firearms 5, rifle specialization. In the end I just decided to go with full size stat blocks, but only give what the character actually needs rather than fiddling with dozens of 1 and 2 dot stats. The hitman has firearms, stealth, a bit of brawl, and athletics, nothing else matters. It makes for very incomplete stat blocks, but npcs don't really need numbers assigned to everything. My biggest struggle right now is just figuring out what are good attribute totals for creatures of different power levels. What do attributes for a BP 8 vampire look like compared to a BP 2 vampire. Would there really be that much of a difference?</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, yeah, now i remember that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-31T03:56:20-07:00","id":1507046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowdragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1506776-stat-blocks-in-city-books#post1506776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All of the city books I've seen have full stat blocks for npcs. Is this really the preference, or is it kind of a waste of space? Would abbreviated stat blocks with common dice pools be better for a city book, especially one with lots of npcs, or would you be disappointed if you got a book that only had abbreviated stats?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would be a bit sad. Though you don't need most stats for mechanics, I find they give a very dense and complex picture of a character that you don't get with normal text. The dicepool system does something similar, but it tends to focus on the highlights of an NPC, rather than the flaws or small details.<br /> <br /> (Admittedly, a lot of those quirks aren't necessarily present in the stat block, it's just that it serves as a good springboard for the imagination.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}